  "notes": "A Compton MC recorded over East Coast sample production, and the research is explicit that the Dre-produced tracks are *outside* this entry — so nothing here is g-funk, even though `relatedGenres` names it. The distinctives are all scale: a big kick anchored on 1 and 3 rather than 1 and 3& with `syncopation` down to 0.2, orchestral crash and timpani accents as `crash`/`tom`/`tomLow` perc lanes, an open voicing spanning 35 semitones for the strings and choir, and the widest `velocityRampRange` in this batch. The 4-bar loop is i–VI–III–VII with I–IV–V for the gospel singles. ⚠ The i–VI–VII family at weight 2 is a REDUCTION of the researched four-chord family, not a separate claim. ⚠ The sustained synth sub with an occasional slow glide is `mirror_kick` at 0.9 with `glideProb` 0.16 — the glide is researched, the mirror is the engine's honest substitute for a held note. ⚠ `medium`: the research documents the production roster, not the sessions, so every drum number here is roster-level inference.",
